  "radioEverydayTitle": "Licence-free radio: PMR446 and Freenet",
  "radioEverydayIntro": "The two bands many households actually own. They need no registration and no examination — and no infrastructure: device to device, one to a few kilometres. That is exactly why they belong here beside CB and amateur radio.",
  "radioPmrTitle": "PMR446",
  "radioPmrRange": "446.0–446.2 MHz",
  "radioPmrChannels": "16 analogue channels, 12.5 kHz spacing",
  "radioPmrPower": "At most 0.5 W ERP",
  "radioPmrAntenna": "Built-in antennas only",
  "radioPmrPeerToPeer": "Device to device only. No fixed station, no repeater, no linking into a network.",
  "radioPmrSource": "Bundesnetzagentur, Vfg. 91/2025 (collective allocation for short-range devices), band 83. Replaces Vfg. 46/2020, valid until 31 December 2035. The channel plan itself is in the harmonised standard, not in the allocation.",
  "radioFreenetTitle": "Freenet Deutschland",
  "radioFreenetRange": "149.01875–149.11875 MHz",
  "radioFreenetAnalogue": "6 channels at 12.5 kHz, analogue or digital",
  "radioFreenetDigital": "Plus 12 channels at 6.25 kHz, digital only",
  "radioFreenetPower": "At most 1 W ERP. Within 10 km of the Belgian and Polish borders, only 0.5 W.",
  "radioFreenetHandheld": "Handheld radios with their own power supply, operable in one hand. Fixed stations are not permitted.",
  "radioFreenetAntenna": "Only the built-in antenna or an exchangeable one on the radio itself. An antenna on a coaxial cable or a mast is not allowed.",
  "radioFreenetPeerToPeer": "Device to device only. No repeater, no relay, no gateway to the internet.",
  "radioFreenetDuration": "No continuous transmission. The standard cuts off after 180 seconds; below that too, transmit only as long as needed.",
  "radioFreenetGermanyOnly": "This allocation applies in Germany only.",
  "radioFreenetExtras": "VOX and CTCSS are expressly permitted.",
  "radioFreenetSource": "Bundesnetzagentur, Vfg. 45/2025, corrected by Mitt. 193/2025. In force since 1 October 2025, valid until 30 September 2035; replaces Vfg. 60/2019.",
  "radioCallingChannelTitle": "There is no official calling channel",
  "radioCallingChannelNone": "Neither PMR446 nor Freenet has an emergency or calling channel laid down by the regulator. What exists are conventions among operators — and they are not uniform.",
  "radioCallingChannelThree": "The most widespread is the private “Channel 3” initiative: PMR446 446.03125 MHz, Freenet 149.0500 MHz, CB 26.985 MHz. One number for all three bands. Elsewhere channel 1 is used instead.",
  "radioCallingChannelNoListener": "Do not count on anybody listening. Nobody is obliged to monitor any of these channels.",
